# Start the services first (Bff.Services, port 5210), then this BFF (port 5115).
# The most telling: open http://localhost:5115 in a browser (alice / demo).
# Here, the REST client keeps the session cookie between requests, like a browser.
@web = http://localhost:5115
@services = http://localhost:5210
@alice = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@bob = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222

### Without a session: 401 (and not a redirect to a login page)
GET {{web}}/api/dashboard
X-CSRF: 1

### Login: the response only contains an HttpOnly cookie, no token
POST {{web}}/bff/login
X-CSRF: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "user": "alice", "password": "demo" }

### Dashboard: 1 request, 7 calls to the services (see X-Downstream-Calls, X-Total-Duration-Ms, X-Downstream-Cumulative-Ms)
GET {{web}}/api/dashboard
X-CSRF: 1

### Without the X-CSRF header: refused, even with a valid session
POST {{web}}/api/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 25 }

### With the header: transfer done, with Alice's token kept on the server side
POST {{web}}/api/transfers
X-CSRF: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{alice}}", "target": "{{bob}}", "amount": 25 }

### Debit Bob's account: 403, the services check the rights (the BFF has no special privilege)
POST {{web}}/api/transfers
X-CSRF: 1
Content-Type: application/json

{ "source": "{{bob}}", "target": "{{alice}}", "amount": 25 }

### ─── Degradation: the offers service goes down ───
PUT {{services}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "offersDown": true }

### The dashboard is displayed anyway: "offers": null, "degraded": ["offers"]
GET {{web}}/api/dashboard
X-CSRF: 1

###
PUT {{services}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "offersDown": false }

### Slower services: the total duration follows the slowest call, not the sum
PUT {{services}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latencyMs": 400 }

###
GET {{web}}/api/dashboard
X-CSRF: 1

###
PUT {{services}}/chaos
Content-Type: application/json

{ "latencyMs": 120 }

### Logout: the session is deleted on the server side
POST {{web}}/bff/logout
X-CSRF: 1

### The services refuse a direct call without a token: only the BFF (with the user's token) gets in
GET {{services}}/profiles/me
